{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":5762,"ns":0,"title":"Civil engineering","extract":"Civil engineering is a professional engineering discipline that deals with the design, construction, and maintenance of the physical and naturally built environment, including public works such as roads, bridges, canals, dams, airports, sewage systems, pipelines, structural components of buildings, and railways.\nCivil engineering is traditionally broken into a number of sub-disciplines.","description":"Engineering discipline focused on physical infrastructure","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}